   "confidence": "low",
   "notes": "Silver Street north side, running east to the Trumpington Street corner. From the west: white-painted shop with black 'Barber Shop' fascia; a four-storey yellow gault-brick Georgian terrace with round-arched doorways with fanlights, multi-pane sashes and wrought-iron balconettes at first floor; then the red-brick Ede & Ravenscroft building (about the last 12 m): two shopfronts with black fascias, gold lettering ('Est 1689', 'EDE & RAVENSCROFT') and green awnings between red-brick piers, a door on the canted corner, and two stacked white timber canted oriels (first and second floors) with roughcast panels between, attic dormers. Terrace bay positions are rough because the Silver Street views are very oblique; the Ede & Ravenscroft part comes from a near-frontal view from the south-east."
